<article class="env-lemma" id="0D5V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D5V">Lemma <span data-tag="0D5V">20.32.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a ringed space. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subspace. For $K$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ we have $H^ p(U, K) = H^ p(U, K|_ U)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{I}^\bullet $ be a K-injective complex of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules representing $K$. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ q(U, K) = H^ q(\Gamma (U, \mathcal{I}^\bullet )) = H^ q(\Gamma (U, \mathcal{I}^\bullet |_ U))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by construction of cohomology. By Lemma <a href="/tag/08BS" data-tag="08BS">20.32.1</a> the complex $\mathcal{I}^\bullet |_ U$ is a K-injective complex representing $K|_ U$ and the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>